id: super-regeneration-unending
name: Unending
order: 2
slot: trait
stacks: 2
description: >
  You are impossible to destroy, and similarly impossible to exhaust.
text: >
  Unending (2): You are impossible to destroy, and similarly impossible to exhaust.
  (1)-[Passive]: You may use an effect with the [Triggered/Defeated] Keyword an additional time per Combat Encounter, but you can still only use the same effect once per Combat Encounter.
  (2)-[Passive]: While you are in the Healthy Health Threshold, double the bonuses from the second effect of Rubbery Body.
  (3)-[Triggered, 1/Encounter]: If you receive Damage from an Attacking Maneuver, you may reduce the Damage by your Surgency.

---

# (1) One more Triggered/Defeated effect a Combat Encounter (the Defeated Moment's limit raised - moments-runtime.mjs); each effect still
# once (registry.mjs usesLeft holds a Triggered/Defeated block to one an Encounter).
[passive, effect 1]
defeated.uses += 1;

# (2) In the Healthy Health Threshold, Rubbery Body (2)'s Soak Value and Defense Value 1(T) once more - doubled, where Rubbery Body is had.
[passive, effect 2]
if (holdsTrait("rubbery-body") && !belowThreshold("bruised")) {
    soakValue += 1(T);
    defenseValue += 1(T);
}

# (3) Damage from an Attacking Maneuver, once an Encounter: lowered by your Surgency - ticked in Take Damage's Before the Damage
# (the damage-cut Moment).
[triggered/damage-cut, 1/encounter, effect 3]
damage.cut += surgency;
